USB Wi-Fi / Bluetooth firmware built into the kernel with CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE
(CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE_DIR="firmware"), one blob per file the built-in
NetHunter USB drivers request: ath9k_htc, carl9170, mt7601u, mt76x0u, mt76x2u,
rt2800usb, rt73usb, rtl8192cu, rtl8xxxu, rtl8188eu, rtw88 (8812AU/8814AU/8821CU),
zd1211rw and btrtl. request_firmware() finds them inside the Image, so no
/system or /vendor firmware files are needed and they work on any ROM.

Sources:
- linux-firmware 20261019 for every file except the two below.
- rtl_bt/rtl8822cu_fw.bin: the "Realtech" (v1) epatch, from the NetHunter
  wireless firmware module (MrRob0-X, v2.0). linux-firmware now ships an
  "RTBTCore" (v2) image that this kernel's btrtl.c cannot parse.
- zd1211/*: not in linux-firmware; from the same NetHunter module
  (zd1211-firmware, GPL-2.0).

Licences: LICENSES/ (texts from linux-firmware), per its WHENCE file:
  rtl_bt/*, rtlwifi/*, rtw88/*     LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt
  ath9k_htc/*, htc_*.fw            LICENCE.open-ath9k-htc-firmware, LICENCE.atheros_firmware
  carl9170-1.fw, zd1211/*          GPL-2.0
  mt7601u.bin                      LICENCE.ralink_a_mediatek_company_firmware
  mediatek/*                       LICENCE.mediatek
  rt2870.bin, rt73.bin             LICENCE.ralink-firmware.txt
